#Housing policy

The dormitory policy outlines student accommodation eligibility, fees, and resident conduct rules. Students must apply before the housing deadline and provide proof of enrollment. The residence office assigns rooms based on year, program, and availability. Housing fees include utilities, internet, and shared room maintenance. Residents must comply with quiet hours, visitor rules, and safety inspections. Students who violate policy may be moved to a different room or lose eligibility for future placement. The dormitory policy outlines student accommodation eligibility, fees, and resident conduct rules. Students must apply before the housing deadline and provide proof of enrollment. The residence office assigns rooms based on year, program, and availability. Housing fees include utilities, internet, and shared room maintenance. Residents must comply with quiet hours, visitor rules, and safety inspections. Students who violate policy may be moved to a different room or lose eligibility for future placement. The dormitory policy outlines student accommodation eligibility, fees, and resident conduct rules. Students must apply before the housing deadline and provide proof of enrollment. The residence office assigns rooms based on year, program, and availability. Housing fees include utilities, internet, and shared room maintenance. Residents must comply with quiet hours, visitor rules, and safety inspections. Students who violate policy may be moved to a different room or lose eligibility for future placement. The dormitory policy outlines student accommodation eligibility, fees, and resident conduct rules. Students must apply before the housing deadline and provide proof of enrollment. The residence office assigns rooms based on year, program, and availability. Housing fees include utilities, internet, and shared room maintenance. Residents must comply with quiet hours, visitor rules, and safety inspections. Students who violate policy may be moved to a different room or